# excel-Project-# Sales Performance Dashboard – Year 2014

 ## Project Overview

 The **Sales Performance Dashboard** is an interactive business intelligence dashboard developed to analyze sales performance for the year **2014**. The dashboard provides a consolidated view of sales by salesperson, monthly sales trends, product performance, sales ranges, and regional distribution.

 The objective of this project is to transform sales data into an easy-to-understand visual report that helps users identify sales patterns, high-performing products, and variations in performance over time.

 ## Dashboard Highlights

 The dashboard reports a **total sales value of 18,307** for the selected reporting context. It provides multiple perspectives of the sales data through interactive charts and report filters.

 ### 1\. Sales Performance by Salesperson

 The salesperson analysis shows **Jan Kotas** with total sales of **18,307** in the displayed dashboard view.

 The salesperson filter allows users to switch between different sales representatives and analyze their individual contribution to overall sales performance.

 ### 2\. Monthly Sales Trend

 The sales trend visualization presents the movement of sales throughout 2014.

 Key observations from the displayed trend include:

 - Sales were approximately **2K in January** and increased to around **3K in March**.
- Sales dropped to approximately **0K during April and May**.
- **June recorded the highest monthly sales**, at approximately **5K**.
- Sales declined sharply in July before recovering gradually during August, September, and October.
- November shows another decline.
- Sales increased significantly in **December to approximately 4K**.

 This trend highlights substantial month-to-month variation and identifies **June and December** as important periods in the displayed sales performance.

 ### 3. Sales by Product

 The product analysis identifies the products contributing to the displayed sales total:

 | Product | Sales |
| --- | --- |
| Beer | 7,994 |
| Fruit Cocktail | 6,942 |
| Chocolate | 3,022 |
| Chocolate Biscuits Mix | 350 |

**Beer** represents the largest contribution among the products shown, followed by **Fruit Cocktail** and **Chocolate**. Chocolate Biscuits Mix contributes a comparatively smaller amount.

 Together, Beer and Fruit Cocktail account for approximately **81.6% of the displayed total sales**, indicating that these two products make up a substantial share of the sales value in this dashboard view.

 ### 4\. Sales Range Analysis

 The sales-range visualization shows the displayed **18,307 total sales** within the **0–10,000 sales range category**.

 This provides an additional way of segmenting and understanding the distribution of sales values.

 ### 5\. Regional Analysis

 The dashboard includes a **Region** report controller with the following regions:

 - North
- West
- East
- South

 This filter enables users to interactively analyze the dashboard based on geographical sales regions and examine how regional selection affects the reported sales figures.

